    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/Licensed-Professional-Counselor-I_R-095970-1": {
      "title": "Licensed Professional Counselor I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Licensed Professional Counselor I Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department Student Affairs (Counseling) Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Responsible for providing counseling services to assist students reach their personal, academic and career goals. Promote a healthy campus environment and meet the psychological needs of the University community. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES : Provides individual and group counseling for personal, academic, and career concerns. Engages in counseling related activities including case management, mental health and related seminars, test administration and interpretation, record maintenance, and referral. Provides crisis intervention services and consults with the director about crisis situations. Engages in program development, educational outreach, psychoeducational programming, and evaluation activities. Conducts all duties and responsibilities in accordance with ethical and professional standards and state laws. Works collaboratively with colleagues in and across the institution. Consults with faculty and staff regarding counseling services for students. Engages in professional development activities to enhance professional skills and maintain counselor licensure. Provides service to the university through committee involvement. Utilizes computer technology to support the counseling function. Contributes to the effective team management of all relevant problems, issues, and opportunities. Assist in the oversight of outreach efforts, including the development of material for the delivery of educational and training programs (targeting mental health and wellness issues) and/or classroom and conference presentations. Assist in the oversight and guidance of the daily activities of assigned counseling or social work practicum/internship students. Co-facilitate case supervision and educational training for counseling or social work practicum/internship students.  Assists with establishing and collaborating with community partnerships on and off campus. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES : Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Counseling and Guidance, Social Work, Counseling, Clinical Psychology, or other specialty related to job function. Practical/field placement relevant to college counseling, or supervised experience related to job function. Clinical competency in multicultural counseling. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Adherence to the Ethical Principles and Code of Conduct for the relevant Texas State Licensing Board and all relevant laws of the State of Texas. Eligible for licensure as a Texas Licensed Professional Counselor-Associate (LPC-Associate), Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC), Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT), Licensed Masters Social Worker (LMSW), or Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW). Must maintain licensure for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications Three (3) years’ experience in counseling or a related field Excellent communication skills—oral and written Experience counseling in a college counseling center Experience in career counseling and alcohol/drug use counseling Successful experience in the development and presentation of mental health seminars Successful work experience in counseling all segments of a college campus population Other Requirements Ability to travel and work beyond normal office hours. Ability to maintain confidentiality. SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL: This position generally does not supervise employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted by 08/21/2026 To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, transcripts, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu . BENEFITS (rules, policies, eligibility apply ): From our generous benefits package and professional development opportunities to our retirement programs and our commitment to service excellence, A&M-Texarkana is an engaging and rewarding place to work. Insurance: Medical $0 - $30 per month for Employee Only coverage after university contribution ($920 value) Up to 83% of premium covered by the university: Employee and Spouse Employee and Children Employee and Family coverage Dental & Vision Life Insurance, Accidental D&D, Long Term Disability, Flexible Spending Account and Day Care Spending Account Tuition Benefits: •     Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program •     75% waiver of tuition and fees for full-time employees, their spouses and children Time Off: •     8+ hours of vacation paid time off every month •     8 hours of sick leave paid time off every month •     8 hours of paid time off for birthday leave •     12-15 paid holidays each year Retirement: •     Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) or Optional Retirement Plan (ORP) •     Voluntary Tax Deferred Account/Deferred Compensation Plan Professional Development via LinkedIn Learning Employee Assistance Program On Campus Wellness Opportunities All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/Executive-Director--Institutional-Effectiveness--Research--and-Planning_R-096068-1": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Institutional Effectiveness, Research, and Planning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Executive Director, Institutional Effectiveness, Research, and Planning Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department Academic Affairs and Office of Graduate & International Studies Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness, Research, and Planning provides executive leadership, oversight, and strategic direction for accreditation, assessment, institutional research, planning, continuous improvement activities, and regulatory reporting ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop strategic direction, goals, plans, and policies for various activities associated with institutional effectiveness including assessment, research, planning, and evaluation processes across campus.  Ensure that data are collected and official reports are produced in a timely manner to maintain compliance with Federal, State, System, and University reporting requirements. Develop technologically driven enhancements for providing internal constituents with access to data and information for decision making. Support and coordinate accreditation processes at the institutional (i.e., SACSCoC) and programmatic levels (e.g., CAPTE, CSWE, ABET, AACSB, CCNE) in conjunction with the Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs. Facilitate institutional research activities in the management, analysis, interpretation, and reporting of various data and information including those associated with student success, curriculum development, distance education development, and enrollment forecasting. Develop and lead continuous improvement processes. Analyze University data and prepares reports and executive summaries. Provide guidance, as needed, with analyzing, reporting and disseminating assessment results. Provide leadership and direction for the design, development, and maintenance of a system of longitudinal databases to assist in planning. Administer the budget and oversees the fiscal operations of the department. Oversee the daily operations of the office including the supervision of staff. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. 8 years of related experience. Knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, and presentation applications. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Interpersonal and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. 10 years of related experience. Experience with Federal and State reporting Demonstrated experience working with Power BI and/or Tableau, institutional assessment and accreditation software such as AEFIS, Taskstream, etc. Other Requirements Ability to travel and work beyond normal office hours. Ability to maintain confidentiality. SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL: This position generally supervises employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu . BENEFITS (rules, policies, eligibility apply ): From our generous benefits package and professional development opportunities to our retirement programs and our commitment to service excellence, A&M-Texarkana is an engaging and rewarding place to work. Insurance: Medical $0 - $30 per month for Employee Only coverage after university contribution ($920 value) Up to 83% of premium covered by the university: Employee and Spouse Employee and Children Employee and Family coverage Dental & Vision Life Insurance, Accidental D&D, Long Term Disability, Flexible Spending Account and Day Care Spending Account Tuition Benefits: •     Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program •     75% waiver of tuition and fees for full-time employees, their spouses and children Time Off: •     8+ hours of vacation paid time off every month •     8 hours of sick leave paid time off every month •     8 hours of paid time off for birthday leave •     12-15 paid holidays each year Retirement: •     Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) or Optional Retirement Plan (ORP) •     Voluntary Tax Deferred Account/Deferred Compensation Plan Professional Development via LinkedIn Learning Employee Assistance Program On Campus Wellness Opportunities All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/Infrastructure---Security-Analyst-II_R-095397-1": {
      "title": "Infrastructure & Security Analyst II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Infrastructure & Security Analyst II Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department Division Of Technology And Distance Education Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Under general direction, perform complex and specialized network, infrastructure, and cybersecurity functions including troubleshooting, analysis, research, implementation, and problem resolution. Supports the administration and maintenance of the University's enterprise network infrastructure, cybersecurity operations, cloud and on-premises systems, identity and access management solutions, and technology infrastructure projects. Serves as a technical resource for networking, security, and infrastructure initiatives while assisting with the protection, availability, reliability, and performance of institutional technology services. Eligibility to work in the U.S. is required at the time of hire. No pre-employment sponsorship is authorized for this position. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES:   Network Operations Monitors enterprise network performance and responds to complex network incidents and service disruptions. Analyzes, troubleshoots, tracks, and resolves enterprise network issues involving wired, wireless, and telecommunications systems. Provides Tier II support and assists with Tier III escalation activities. Maintains network topology diagrams, documentation, inventories, and technical standards. Assists with configuration, deployment, and maintenance of switches, wireless infrastructure, firewalls, and network appliances. Identifies unauthorized devices and security concerns within the network environment and coordinates remediation efforts. Supports infrastructure projects involving network expansion, modernization, and technology refresh initiatives. Cybersecurity Operations   Assists with vulnerability management activities including scanning, remediation tracking, patch verification, and reporting. Monitors security alerts, logs, and events from cybersecurity tools and systems. Assists with security incident response, investigation, containment, recovery, and documentation efforts. Supports identity and access management processes including account provisioning, access reviews, multi-factor authentication, and privileged access controls. Collaborates with TAMUS Cybersecurity Shared Services to implement security controls, policies, standards, and best practices. Assists with compliance initiatives related to Texas A&M System standards, State of Texas requirements, cybersecurity audits, and risk assessments. Participates in security awareness and cybersecurity education efforts. Infrastructure Operations Monitors infrastructure performance and availability to ensure reliable operation of enterprise technology services. Assists with disaster recovery, backup validation, and business continuity initiatives. Supports implementation of infrastructure upgrades, migrations, and modernization projects. Maintains technical documentation related to infrastructure systems, configurations, and operational procedures. Project Support & Customer Engagement Works with campus departments to identify technology requirements and recommend appropriate infrastructure and security solutions. Assists project leaders with planning, implementation, testing, and deployment activities. Participates in technology evaluations, proof-of-concept testing, and integration efforts. Provides technical consultation and support to faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Collaborates with vendors and service providers to resolve technical issues and support project initiatives. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Minimum Qualifications  Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Three years of related experience. Knowledge of word processing and spreadsheet applications. Knowledge of word processing and spreadsheet applications. Knowledge of troubleshooting and problem-solving, client relations skills, requirement assessment and analysis, project management methodology, context and interrelationships, and proficiency in Information Technology Interface Library (ITIL) Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Microsoft, Palo Alto, VMware, Cisco, Entra ID, Ruckus, or Intune technologies. Certifications such as Security+, Network+, CCNA, CCNP, Palo Alto, or ITIL.  Knowledge of enterprise networking concepts including routing, switching, wireless communications, firewalls, and network security. Knowledge of cybersecurity principles including vulnerability management, incident response, security monitoring, risk management, and access control. Knowledge of infrastructure technologies including servers, virtualization, cloud platforms, storage systems, backup solutions, and endpoint management. Knowledge of project management methodologies, IT service management practices, and Information Technology Infrastructure Library (ITIL) principles. Ability to manage multiple priorities and projects while maintaining attention to detail. Strong analytical, organizational, problem-solving, and decision-making skills. Other Requirements Availability to respond to critical network, infrastructure, and cybersecurity incidents outside normal business hours. Participation in disaster recovery testing, cybersecurity incident response, and infrastructure maintenance activities. Eligibility to work in the U.S. is required at the time of hire. No pre-employment sponsorship is authorized for this position. Physical Requirements: Exerting up to 30 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 15 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Must be able to frequently move about campus facilities, including traversing stairs, navigating multiple floors, and traveling between buildings to provide on-site technical support. Bending and crouching around and under objects to check, adjust, maintain, install, or repair equipment. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.   SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL :   This position generally does supervise employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted by 08/19/2026 To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu . BENEFITS (rules, policies, eligibility apply ): From our generous benefits package and professional development opportunities to our retirement programs and our commitment to service excellence, A&M-Texarkana is an engaging and rewarding place to work. Insurance: Medical $0 - $30 per month for Employee Only coverage after university contribution ($920 value) Up to 83% of premium covered by the university: Employee and Spouse Employee and Children Employee and Family coverage Dental & Vision Life Insurance, Accidental D&D, Long Term Disability, Flexible Spending Account and Day Care Spending Account Tuition Benefits: •     Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program •     75% waiver of tuition and fees for full-time employees, their spouses and children Time Off: •     8+ hours of vacation paid time off every month •     8 hours of sick leave paid time off every month •     8 hours of paid time off for birthday leave •     12-15 paid holidays each year Retirement: •     Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) or Optional Retirement Plan (ORP) •     Voluntary Tax Deferred Account/Deferred Compensation Plan Professional Development via LinkedIn Learning Employee Assistance Program On Campus Wellness Opportunities All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
