    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/Adjunct-Instructor---Kinesiology_R-095776-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Kinesiology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Instructor - Kinesiology Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department CNHHS - Health Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Nursing, Health, and Human Services CNHHS occasionally has openings for part-time adjunct instructors appointed on a per semester basis.  Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in Kinesiology adds applicants to a pool which is available to the department for selection as needed for Fall 20 26 , Spring 20 27 and/or Summer 20 27 .  Minimum educational requirements for undergraduate level courses: Master’s degree in the teaching discipline or related field, including a minimum of 18 graduate level credit hours in the teaching discipline.  Degree and coursework must be obtained from a regionally accredited institution.  Minimum educational requirements for graduate level courses: Doctorate or terminal degree in the teaching discipline, or closely related field, including a minimum of 18 graduate level credit hours in the teaching discipline.  Degree and coursework must be obtained from a regionally accredited institution.   Duties: Required to teach Kinesiology course(s) in one or more of the following modalities:  Face-to-face, web-enhanced, hybrid, or online .  Courses may be conducted as a 5-week, 8-week, 10-week or 16-week term depending on the semester.  Must coordinate course administrative duties such as, but not limited to, grading student work, loading all course content, such as assessments and lecture modules, meeting with students, submitting grades in a timely manner, meeting census and grade deadlines, and additional administrative duties as needed. Compensation: $ 2400 per undergraduate section taught with a master’s degree; $2900 per undergraduate section taught with a Ph D. $3600 per graduate level section taught.  The following items must be uploaded with your application: Resume and/or CV Copy of graduate level transcripts At least two (2) professional references Once you submit your application, you will not be able to revise or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu .   TAMUT only accepts online applications and documents. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/End-User-Support-Specialist-I_R-095480": {
      "title": "End User Support Specialist I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title End User Support Specialist I Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department Division Of Technology And Distance Education Proposed Minimum Salary $3,333.33 monthly Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The End User Support Specialist I, under general supervision, provides Tier 2 end-user technology support to faculty, staff, students, and other campus users to ensure the efficient, reliable, and secure use of university technology resources. This position troubleshoots and resolves routine to moderately complex hardware, software, account access, connectivity, classroom technology, lab technology, printing, and peripheral support issues across supported Windows, Apple, mobile, and other computing environments. This position is responsible for documenting, prioritizing, updating, resolving, and escalating Service Desk tickets in accordance with departmental procedures and service expectations. The End User Support Specialist I assists with endpoint deployments, software installations, classroom and lab technology support, user training, knowledge base documentation, and technology refresh initiatives. This position also provides professional customer service, follows established technical standards, supports compliance with university policies, and contributes to the continuous improvement of Service Desk operations. Salary information: The expected salary for this position is $40,000.00 annually. Eligibility to work in the U.S. is required at the time of hire. No pre-employment sponsorship is authorized for this position. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Provides front-line technical support and resolves routine to moderately complex end-user technology issues for end users across Apple, Windows, mobile, classroom, lab, and other supported computing environments. Troubleshoots a variety of hardware, software, account access, printing, network connectivity, classroom technology, and peripheral issues. Receives, documents, prioritizes, updates, and resolves Service Desk tickets in the designated IT service management system. Ensures that all Service Desk interactions are accurately logged, categorized, and updated with clear troubleshooting notes, resolution details, and customer communication. Evaluates Tier 2 support issues and follows them through to resolution or appropriate escalation. Performs initial diagnosis, researches known issues, applies documented solutions, and escalates tickets when additional technical expertise, system access, or vendor support is required. Provides timely, professional, and customer-focused support to faculty, staff, students, and other campus users. Communicates clearly with customers regarding issue status, next steps, expected timelines, and resolution outcomes. Installs, configures, deploys, and supports end-user hardware and software, including desktops, laptops, classroom computers, lab computers, printers, peripherals, standard campus applications, and approved specialized software. Assists with new technology deployments, computer replacements, software rollouts, device setup, and post-deployment support. Provides guidance and recommendations to end users regarding the appropriate use, selection, and operation of supported hardware, software, and technology resources in accordance with university policies, standards, accessibility requirements, security requirements, and departmental procedures. Supports classroom, lab, conference room, and distance learning technology, including equipment setup, routine checks, preventative maintenance, troubleshooting, and coordination with faculty and staff to facilitate instructional use of technology. Provides training and assistance to end users on widely used campus applications, specialized software, classroom technology, collaboration tools, and standard IT services. Develops, updates, and maintains internal documentation, user-facing knowledge base articles, frequently asked questions, troubleshooting guides, and support procedures related to end-user computing and Service Desk operations. Assists in identifying recurring issues, service gaps, documentation needs, and opportunities for process improvement. Provides status updates, resource estimates, and progress reports as requested. Provides technical input and recommendations for the planning, acquisition, configuration, and implementation of new computer hardware, software, classroom technology, and end-user technology solutions. Participates in departmental projects, technology refreshes, campus initiatives, committees, and working groups as assigned. Provides support for technical standards, service procedures, deployment planning, and operational readiness. Ensures assigned work is completed accurately, professionally, and in compliance with departmental standards, project requirements, university policies, security expectations, and applicable quality standards. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Four months of related experience. Knowledge of word processing and spreadsheet applications. Knowledge of advanced IT, intermediate troubleshooting, client relations, formulating and contributing ideas, and knowledge of the Information Technology Interface Library (ITIL). Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Preferred Qualifications Two years of related experience providing technical support in an IT Service Desk, help desk, desktop support, classroom technology, or end-user support environment. Operational knowledge of Windows, macOS, mobile operating systems, and commonly used desktop computing hardware and software. Experience troubleshooting end-user hardware, software, account access, printing, network connectivity, peripheral, classroom technology, or lab technology issues. Experience documenting, updating, and resolving support requests in an IT service management or ticketing system. Knowledge of desktop computing security procedures, including password security, multi-factor authentication, software compliance, data protection, and safe handling of university-owned technology assets. Experience installing, configuring, deploying, or supporting computers, software applications, printers, peripherals, classroom computers, or lab technology. Experience creating or maintaining technical documentation, knowledge base articles, frequently asked questions, or internal support procedures. Familiarity with higher education technology environments, instructional technology, classroom support, distance learning technology, or academic lab support. Relevant technical certification or training, such as CompTIA A+, Network+, ITIL Foundation, Microsoft, Apple, Google, or other related technology support certification. Other Requirements Excellent written and verbal communication, analytical, interpersonal, organizational, and customer service skills. Ability to occasionally work outside normal business hours, including evenings or weekends, to support system maintenance, technology deployments, campus events, semester startup activities, emergency response, or other operational needs. Physical Requirements: Exerting up to 30 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 15 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Must be able to frequently move about campus facilities, including traversing stairs, navigating multiple floors, and traveling between buildings to provide on-site technical support. Bending and crouching around and under objects to check, adjust, maintain, install, or repair equipment. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL: This position generally does not supervise employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted by 08/01/2026 To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu . BENEFITS (rules, policies, eligibility apply ): From our generous benefits package and professional development opportunities to our retirement programs and our commitment to service excellence, A&M-Texarkana is an engaging and rewarding place to work. Insurance: Medical $0 - $30 per month for Employee Only coverage after university contribution ($920 value) Up to 83% of premium covered by the university: Employee and Spouse Employee and Children Employee and Family coverage Dental & Vision Life Insurance, Accidental D&D, Long Term Disability, Flexible Spending Account and Day Care Spending Account Tuition Benefits: •     Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program •     75% waiver of tuition and fees for full-time employees, their spouses and children Time Off: •     8+ hours of vacation paid time off every month •     8 hours of sick leave paid time off every month •     8 hours of paid time off for birthday leave •     12-15 paid holidays each year Retirement: •     Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) or Optional Retirement Plan (ORP) •     Voluntary Tax Deferred Account/Deferred Compensation Plan Professional Development via LinkedIn Learning Employee Assistance Program On Campus Wellness Opportunities All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
