    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/Adjunct-Instructor---Business_R-093360-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Instructor - Business Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department CBET - Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Anita and Truman Arnold College of Business occasionally has openings for part-time adjunct instructors appointed on a per semester basis.  Applying for a part-time teaching appointment in Business adds applicants to a pool which is available to the business division for selection as needed for Fall 2026, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027.  Minimum requirements due to accreditations Minimum educational requirements (SACSCOC) for undergraduate level courses: Master’s degree in the teaching discipline or related field, including a minimum of 18 graduate level credit hours in the teaching discipline.  Degree and coursework must be obtained from a regionally accredited institution.  Minimum educational requirements (SACSCOC) for graduate level courses: Doctorate or terminal degree in the teaching discipline, or closely related field, including a minimum of 18 graduate level credit hours in the teaching discipline.  Degree and coursework must be obtained from a regionally accredited institution.   Minimum requirements faculty qualification (AACSB) : Must have the appropriate initial qualification and appropriate maintenance of qualification for the last six-year period in the field of teaching to be qualified per AACSB standard 3 of the new 2026 Global Standards for Business Education. Duties: Required to teach business course(s) in one or more of the following business disciplines: accounting, business law, agribusiness, economics, entrepreneurship, finance, general business (including areas such as introduction to business, business communication, international business), management (including areas such as human resources, operations, supply chain, technology management), marketing, and/or sports management. Required to teach course(s) in one or more of the following modalities :  Face-to-face, web-enhanced, hybrid, or online.  Courses may be conducted as a 5-week, 8-week, 10-week or 16-week term depending on the semester.  Must coordinate course administrative duties such as, but not limited to, grading student work, loading all course content, such as assessments and lecture modules, meeting with students, submitting grades in a timely manner, meeting census and grade deadlines, and additional administrative duties as needed. Compensation: $3,300 per undergraduate section taught with a master’s degree; $3,800 per undergraduate section taught with a Ph D., $4,000 per graduate level section taught with a master’s degree, and $4,500 per graduate level section taught with a PhD.  The following items must be uploaded with your application: Resume and/or CV Copy of graduate level transcripts. If international it must be credentialed (e.g. by WES) At least two (2) professional references Once you submit your application, you will not be able to revise or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu .   TAMUT only accepts online applications and documents. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana-TX/Residence-Life-Coordinator_R-091943-1": {
      "title": "Residence Life Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Residence Life Coordinator Agency Texas A&M University - Texarkana Department Student Affairs BLV Proposed Minimum Salary $3,416.66 monthly Job Location Texarkana, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Responsible for providing individual and group educational and developmental opportunities; maintaining residential facilities that are clean, safe and in order; managing operations to include planning, fiscal matters, and personnel relations. Serve as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) for Clery reporting purposes.  Salary information: The expected salary for this position is $41,000.00 annually. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Community Development & Student Support Cultivate a positive and engaging residential community that promotes student involvement, personal development, and academic success within the assigned area. Design and implement educational and social initiatives aligned with the residential curriculum, utilizing assessment data and community trends to inform programming decisions and improve engagement outcomes. Maintain a visible and accessible presence within the residence hall, proactively engaging students, addressing concerns, and connecting residents with appropriate campus resources. Supervision & Staff Development Assist with recruiting, training, supervising and evaluating Resident Assistants and assigned student employees, establishing clear performance expectations and accountability measures. Participate in ongoing staff development through regular meetings, structured training initiatives, and performance feedback to ensure effective community leadership. Coordinate duty coverage and response protocols to ensure consistent supervision and appropriate support within the residential community. Residential Operations & Administration Direct the day-to-day operations of the assigned residential area, including occupancy transitions, check-ins, check-outs, and community readiness processes in alignment with departmental procedures. Manage accurate administrative documentation and analyze community-level data related to occupancy, incidents, and engagement trends to inform operational adjustments. Support large-scale departmental initiatives such as move-in, move-out, room changes, summer housing, and camps and conferences to ensure coordinated and efficient execution. Maintain proficiency in departmental and university systems used to manage housing operations, student records, conduct documentation, and reporting functions (e.g., StarRez, Banner, Maxient, Microsoft Office, and other applicable financial databases). Facilities & Community Standards Monitor building conditions and coordinate maintenance, custodial, and safety concerns with campus partners to ensure a clean, functional, and well-maintained residential environment. Conduct routine health, safety, and risk management inspections, educating residents on community standards and emergency procedures. Student Conduct, & Crisis Response Participate in an on-call rotation and respond to student crises, behavioral concerns, and emergencies, providing appropriate support and follow-up. Address student conduct matters at the community level using educational interventions, documenting incidents and referring cases when appropriate. Department, Division, & Professional Commitments Collaborate with campus partners and university departments to strengthen student support networks and represent the residential community in cross-functional initiatives as assigned. Contribute to departmental planning and assessment efforts by providing community-level insights and participating in operational improvement initiatives. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. One year of related experience. Knowledge of word processing and spreadsheet applications. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills.   Preferred Qualifications Experience with university/college housing (i.e., lived in, resident assistant, graduate assistant, etc.) Master's degree in student personnel, higher education, counseling, or a related area. Prior residence life professional experience Experience in staff supervision, administration of residence hall operations, and facilitating student development programming activities.     Experience working effectively with various student populations Other Requirements Position requires evening and weekend availability as operational needs dictate. Live-on position requiring primary residence in assigned on-campus housing and participation in the university meal plan (provided). SUPERVISION OF PERSONNEL: This position generally supervises personnel, such as student workers/part-time employees. OPEN UNTIL FILLED. To apply: Upload your cover letter, CV/resume, and 3 professional reference's contact information with one reference being a supervisor/manager in the questionnaire section of your application. Please remember once you submit your application you will not be able to “revise” or upload any documents. If you have any questions about uploading or a revision to your application, you may contact HR@tamut.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
